# ---- runtime / build ----
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
.pnpm-store/

# ---- local state written by the runtime ----
# States are committed per transition into a JSONL ledger (docs/STATE.md §5).
# Never commit a real run's ledger, but keep the fixtures.
#
# AND keep the DEVELOPMENT TRACE. `*.jsonl` was meant for runtime ledgers and
# silently swallowed traces/ too, so the trace system documented as append-only
# evidence sat untracked through four commits -- 64 records not in version
# control, not backed up, and invisible to anyone else. Found by asking whether
# the file was actually in HEAD rather than assuming the commit had taken it.
# See docs/MISTAKES.md: a corpus you believe is recorded and is not.
*.jsonl
!tests/fixtures/**/*.jsonl
!traces/**/*.jsonl
# Raw rows behind a research report are evidence of the same kind as traces/,
# and the blanket rule swallowed them the same way: `l1-head-to-head.jsonl`
# (380 rows, cited from docs/research/L1_HEAD_TO_HEAD.md) and
# `decision-variants.jsonl` (3,040 rows, cited from
# docs/research/DECISION_DECOMPOSITION_2026.md) were both on disk and invisible
# to version control. Keep measured research rows; the runtime-ledger intent
# stands for everything else.
!docs/research/**/*.jsonl
.consonance/
/tmp/

# ---- credentials: MUST never be committed ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.credentials.yaml
secrets/
**/credentials.json

# ---- editor / OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ---- logs / coverage ----
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcoveralls

# ---- local scratch ----
scratch/
tmp/

# Scratch for the Consonance convergence working session: an unzipped copy of
# the source .docx (word/*.xml, docProps/, customXml/) plus extracted text and
# the delta/agenda notes. The .docx original lives outside the repo; none of
# this is repository material.
.tmp-consonance/
